.TH LE-HARNESS 1 "November 2026" "le-harness 0.1.0-rc.5" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
le-harness \- transparent coding-agent runtime for the Mistral ecosystem
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B le-harness
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.I COMMAND
.RI [ COMMAND-OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Le Harness runs bounded coding-agent sessions with transactional edits,
explicit permission policies, Mistral chat and fill-in-the-middle requests,
optional loopback-local models, MCP clients, and inspectable session traces.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B doctor
Print build and runtime diagnostics. With
.BR --live ,
query the configured Mistral endpoint.
.TP
.B auth
Save, inspect, or remove the Mistral API key in the native OS credential store.
.TP
.B run
Run one bounded coding-agent session.
.TP
.B eval
Run a repeatable evaluation manifest.
.TP
.B session
List, inspect, or validate resumability of persisted session journals.
.TP
.B tui
Explore a persisted execution trace in an interactive terminal UI.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --no-input
Disable credential prompts and interactive action approvals.
.TP
.B --no-credential-store
Do not read or save API keys in the native OS credential store.
.TP
.B -h, --help
Print command help.
.TP
.B -V, --version
Print the installed version.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MISTRAL_API_KEY
Mistral API credential. If absent during an interactive cloud command, Le
Harness reuses a saved credential or requests hidden input and saves it in the
native OS credential store.
.TP
.B LE_HARNESS_CHAT_MODEL
Exact cloud planner/chat model identifier.
.TP
.B LE_HARNESS_FIM_MODEL
Exact cloud fill-in-the-middle model identifier.
.TP
.B LE_HARNESS_UTILITY_MODEL
Optional utility model identifier; defaults to the chat model.
.TP
.B LE_HARNESS_STATE_DIR
Parent directory for persisted session journals.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/le-harness/sessions
Default session journal directory when
.B LE_HARNESS_STATE_DIR
is not set.
.SH SECURITY
Native command execution is bounded but is not a security sandbox. Use the
Docker execution backend for automated execution and review its daemon and
image trust boundary separately.
.SH SEE ALSO
Project documentation is installed under
.IR /usr/share/doc/le-harness/ .
The upstream project is available at
.IR https://github.com/artemidius/Le-Harness .
